   "source": [
    "# Central Dogma Demo\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains code capable of running a demo on the Central Dogma of molecular biology, a framework which describes the flow of genetic information from DNA to RNA to proteins.\n",
    "\n",
    "As part of this demo, there are three functions: two functions handle transcription of DNA into RNA, and one function handles the translation of RNA into proteins.\n",
    "\n",
    "Finally, this notebook contains code for a custom CentralDogma class. Objects created from this class contain **methods** which carry out transcription and translation. Results from calling these methods are stored as the object's **attributes**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f4d30d7-a8fe-4b49-93c6-63ef43522e06",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
