   "source": [
    "## Running the Demo\n",
    "\n",
    " To continue with our demo, we define two more custom functions in the cell below:\n",
    " 1. <code>transcribe_to_RNA()</code> which takes a template DNA string as input and returns the encoded mRNA string as its output\n",
    " 2. <code>translate_to_protein()</code> which takes an mRNA string and a tRNA dictionary as inputs and returns the encoded protein string as its output\n",
    "\n",
    "**Take a moment to read each function's docstring to understand what each function does, and briefly scan the code to see how these functions are implemented in python.**\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: For extra code tracing practice, describe the numbered lines of code in the cell below*: "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "0a665b67-cacd-4e39-9e90-7873d594ef08",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def transcribe_to_RNA(DNA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Creates mRNA from template DNA\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Template DNA is passed through the create_complement_string()\n",
    "    function and Thymine is replaced with Uracil. Invalid bases result\n",
    "    in the destruction of the mRNA. Valid mRNA strings are converted\n",
    "    to lower-case before being returned\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        DNA (str): Template DNA strand\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        mRNA (str): mRNA encoded by template DNA\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    complement = create_complement_string(DNA)                     #1\n",
    "    mRNA = complement.replace('T', 'U')\n",
    "    if 'X' in mRNA:                                                #2\n",
    "        print('RNA destroyed via post-transcriptional control')    #3\n",
    "    else:                                                          #4\n",
    "        mRNA = mRNA.lower() \n",
    "        return mRNA                                                #5\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def translate_to_protein(mRNA, tRNA):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Translate mRNA to protein\n",
    "\n",
    "    mRNA transcripts are first checked for start and stop\n",
    "    sequences and total length. Invalid mRNA sequences will\n",
    "    result in early termination.\n",
    "\n",
    "    This function uses the tRNA dictionary to translate \n",
    "    valid mRNA sequences into proteins based on the amino\n",
    "    acids encoded by each codon. Translation ends once\n",
    "    a stop codon is reached\n",
    "\n",
    "    Args:\n",
    "        mRNA (str): mRNA transcript to translate\n",
    "        tRNA (dict): Stores amino acids values accessed via mRNA keys\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns:\n",
    "        protein (str): Amino acid sequence encoded by mRNA\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    if mRNA[0:3] != 'aug':                                      #1\n",
    "        print(\"This sequence does not have a start codon \\n\")   \n",
    "    elif mRNA[-3:] not in ['uaa', 'uag', 'uga']:                #2\n",
    "        print(\"This sequence does not have a stop codon \\n\")    \n",
    "    elif len(mRNA) % 3 != 0:                                    #3\n",
    "        print(\"Incomplete sequence \\n\")                         \n",
    "    else:                                                       #4\n",
    "        elongation = True                                       #5\n",
    "        print(\"Initiating translation...\")\n",
    "        cycle_num = 0                                           #6\n",
    "        protein = ''\n",
    "        while elongation:                                      #7\n",
    "            start = 3 * cycle_num                              #8\n",
    "            stop = 3 * (cycle_num + 1)                         #9\n",
    "            codon = mRNA[start:stop]                           #10\n",
    "            amino = tRNA[codon]                                #11\n",
    "            print(f\"{codon}, {amino}\")\n",
    "            if amino == 'STOP':                                #12\n",
    "                elongation = False                             #13\n",
    "                print(\"Translation terminated.\\n\")\n",
    "                return protein                                 #14\n",
    "            else:                                              #15\n",
    "                protein += amino                               #16\n",
    "                cycle_num += 1                                 #17"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c5602443-0dff-4a21-8982-b944ab4091c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "As a reminder, our function <code>translate_to_protein()</code> requires two input arguments (<code>mRNA</code> and <code>tRNA</code>). In the cell below, we'll define a dictionary called <code>tRNA</code> that uses mRNA codons as keys and stores one-letter abbreviations of amino acids as values.\n",
    "\n",
    "This dictionary was created using information found [here](https://www.khanacademy.org/test-prep/mcat/biomolecules/x04f6bc56:transcription-and-translation/a/mrna-code-and-translation) and [here](https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Amino-acid-abbreviations_tbl1_301887506)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "5d6a5c16-346b-4bc0-abfd-1c82a63ad024",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tRNA = {'uuu': 'F', 'uuc': 'F', 'uua': 'L', 'uug': 'L',\n",
    "       'ucu': 'S', 'ucc': 'S', 'uca': 'S', 'ucg': 'S',\n",
    "       'uau': 'Y', 'uac': 'Y', 'uaa': 'STOP', 'uag': 'STOP',\n",
    "       'ugu': 'C', 'ugc': 'C', 'uga': 'STOP', 'ugg': 'W',\n",
    "\n",
    "       'cuu': 'L', 'cuc': 'L', 'cua': 'L', 'cug': 'L',\n",
    "       'ccu': 'P', 'ccc': 'P', 'cca': 'P', 'ccg': 'P',\n",
    "       'cau': 'H', 'cac': 'H', 'caa': 'Q', 'cag': 'Q',\n",
    "       'cgu': 'R', 'cgc': 'R', 'cga': 'R', 'cgg': 'R',\n",
    "\n",
    "       'auu': 'I', 'auc': 'I', 'aua': 'I', 'aug': 'M',\n",
    "       'acu': 'T', 'acc': 'T', 'aca': 'T', 'acg': 'T',\n",
    "       'aau': 'N', 'aac': 'N', 'aaa': 'K', 'aag': 'K',\n",
    "       'agu': 'S', 'agc': 'S', 'aga': 'R', 'agg': 'R', \n",
    "\n",
    "       'guu': 'I', 'guc': 'I', 'gua': 'I', 'gug': 'M',\n",
    "       'gcu': 'T', 'gcc': 'T', 'gca': 'T', 'gcg': 'T',\n",
    "       'gau': 'N', 'gac': 'N', 'gaa': 'K', 'gag': 'K',\n",
    "       'ggu': 'S', 'ggc': 'S', 'gga': 'R', 'ggg': 'R' \n",
    "       }"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce17e8d5-2599-43bd-8c66-20db2ddacb10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "With our functions designed and our dictionary created, we can finally put our demo together. To do this, we'll use an object-oriented approach. This means that we will define as custom class that we can use to initialize an object capable of transcribing DNA into RNA and translating RNA into protein.\n",
    "\n",
    "**To create this class in python, we use the following syntax:**\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>class CentralDogma():</code>\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that creating a class involves using **the python keyword** <code>class</code> followed by **the name of our class**, **paretheses** <code>()</code> and a **colon** <code>:</code>.\n",
    "\n",
    "The object that we create with this class has **attributes** that store information and **methods** that perform functions on the object's attributes. A special method found in most classes is the <code>__init__()</code> method which initializes the values of attributes stored in the class object. The first argument in this method is always <code>self</code> followed by whatever input arguments you would like your class to accept. For our CentralDogma class we have:\n",
    "\n",
    "<code> def \_\_init\_\_(self, DNA, tRNA): </code>\n",
    "\n",
    "This means that when we create a new object from our CentralDogma class, we'll need to pass in <code>DNA</code> and <code>tRNA</code> variables as input arguments:\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>CD_object = CentralDogma(DNA = DNA, tRNA = tRNA)</code>\n",
    "\n",
    "In addition to our <code>\_\_init\_\_()</code> method, our CentralDogma class has two other methods <code>transcribe</code> and <code>translate</code> that update the <code>self.mRNA</code> and <code>self.protein</code> attributes respectively.\n",
    "\n",
    "Assuming that we initialized our object with the variable name <code>CD_object</code>, we can access its attributes using the following syntax:\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>stored_DNA = CD_object.DNA</code>\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>stored_tRNA = CD_object.tRNA</code>\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>stored_mRNA = CD_object.mRNA</code>\n",
    "\n",
    "<code>stored_protein = CD_object.protein</code>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "735083e5-03d2-4aa4-a58c-8b5a4bb2f7eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Run the cell below to define our custom class:**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "1b5610be-0af4-459e-a5fc-c8c01a5932ab",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CentralDogma():                                                              #1\n",
    "    def __init__(self, DNA, tRNA):                                                 #2\n",
    "        self.DNA = DNA                                                             #3\n",
    "        self.tRNA = tRNA\n",
    "        self.mRNA = None\n",
    "        self.protein = None\n",
    "\n",
    "    def transcribe(self):                                                          #4                                     \n",
    "        self.mRNA = transcribe_to_RNA(self.DNA)                                    #5\n",
    "        return self                                                                #6\n",
    "\n",
    "    def translate(self):                                                           #7\n",
    "        if self.mRNA is not None:                                                  #8\n",
    "            self.protein = translate_to_protein(self.mRNA, self.tRNA)              #9\n",
    "            return self                                        \n",
    "        else:                                                                      #10\n",
    "            self.transcribe()                                                      #11\n",
    "            if self.mRNA is None:                                                  #12\n",
    "                print(\"There is no mRNA to translate\")\n",
    "            else:                                                                  #13\n",
    "                self.protein = translate_to_protein(self.mRNA, self.tRNA)\n",
    "                return self                                                        #14"
   ]
  },
  {
